{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const WINDOWS_MODIFIER_LABELS: Record<CanonicalModifier | \"Mod\", string>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/display-labels.ts#L68","children":[{"type":"text","value":"display-labels.ts:68"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier key labels for Windows/Linux display."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Used by formatting functions to display hotkeys with standard text labels\n(e.g., 'Ctrl' for Control, 'Win' for Meta/Windows key) instead of symbols.\nThis provides a familiar Windows/Linux look and feel in hotkey displays."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"STANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Control'] // 'Ctrl'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Meta'] // 'Win'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Alt'] // 'Alt'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Shift'] // 'Shift'","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst WINDOWS_MODIFIER_LABELS: Record<CanonicalModifier | \"Mod\", string>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [display-labels.ts:68](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/display-labels.ts#L68)\n\nModifier key labels for Windows/Linux display.\n\nUsed by formatting functions to display hotkeys with standard text labels\n(e.g., 'Ctrl' for Control, 'Win' for Meta/Windows key) instead of symbols.\nThis provides a familiar Windows/Linux look and feel in hotkey displays.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Control'] // 'Ctrl'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Meta'] // 'Win'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Alt'] // 'Alt'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Shift'] // 'Shift'\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: WINDOWS_MODIFIER_LABELS\ntitle: WINDOWS_MODIFIER_LABELS\n---\n\n```ts\nconst WINDOWS_MODIFIER_LABELS: Record<CanonicalModifier | \"Mod\", string>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [display-labels.ts:68](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/display-labels.ts#L68)\n\nModifier key labels for Windows/Linux display.\n\nUsed by formatting functions to display hotkeys with standard text labels\n(e.g., 'Ctrl' for Control, 'Win' for Meta/Windows key) instead of symbols.\nThis provides a familiar Windows/Linux look and feel in hotkey displays.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Control'] // 'Ctrl'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Meta'] // 'Win'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Alt'] // 'Alt'\nSTANDARD_MODIFIER_LABELS['Shift'] // 'Shift'\n```\n"}
